andidate has a strong academic record, excellent references, and interviewed well, you'd be rejecting them based on a probability, not on their actual demonstrated behavior. That's discriminatory. So no, your observations aren't crazy. But they're also not a free pass to act on a stereotype. The only path forward for your notes is the one I've been pointing to: ignore the tattoos, review the actual qualifications, and document from there.
